{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle","id":266607,"title":"Recruiting for a play-by-post Changeling: the Lost chronicle!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-26T21:44:44-07:00","id":266607,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon14.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Recruiting for a play-by-post Changeling: the Lost chronicle!","content":"So, I haven't gotten any good Lost - or any good STing - in my life in a long time. I figured, now's the time to change that! I've run other games in play-by-post and I've run Lost live, but I've never combined the two, so I figured, what the hey!<br /> <br /> As a storyteller, I enjoy building a world that's effected not only by what the players do, but by what they've done in the past. Backgrounds are a requirement, and backgrounds with plenty of good hooks are a strong plus. Themes can change depending on the story, but I often include difficult choices and unforeseen consequences for the players' actions.<br /> <br /> Now. Game recruitment seems to be a seller's market these days, so I'm going to be picky. I'm aiming to choose people with strong roleplaying, writing, and story-telling skills, because I want to tell an awesome story together. I'm more than a little bit of a grammar fascist, so if you're not 100% sure of your skills, spellcheck Is Your Friend. An ideal intro post will include your preferred playstyle, an example of character-based writing, and (just for fun) why you think you will triumph over your fellows.<br /> <br /> Final game roster will be posted Friday, 10/3.<br /> <br /> Edit: Recruitment is closed! Thanks to everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 11-01-2014, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T23:57:42-07:00","id":266659,"title":"","content":"Cool, but I have a couple of questions: Is this gonna use GMC, and are there any particular house rules(mostly pertaining to character creation)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T02:55:34-07:00","id":266711,"title":"","content":"Damn. I would have been interested, but I don't have time to read the two books before next friday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T09:33:14-07:00","id":266793,"title":"","content":"This will not be using GMC - I haven't had an opportunity to internalize the changes from base WoD and the game hasn't been transitioned over anyway. I haven't decided on any houserules, though any choices (such as dual-kithing with a Shadowsoul) might be subject to ST veto if I think they'll be bad for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T19:47:21-07:00","id":267881,"title":"","content":"I'd have been in for this, but the thought of 'triumphing over your fellows' isn't something I am interested in doing for a Changeling game. Still, I wish this luck, because I love Changeling, being one of my top nWoD splats to play and be a part of. Perhaps I may be interested to join later down the road if a gap forms, I'll be reading this anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T21:57:48-07:00","id":267973,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean &quot;triumphing over your fellows&quot; in game, I meant triumphing over the other applicants for spots *in* the game. <br /> <br /> <br /> ...I may have overestimated the degree to which this is a seller's market...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T15:34:09-07:00","id":268578,"title":"","content":"I think your fatal mistake, HobbitGuy, was the content of your OP. Too much of it explained your pet peeve and not enough of it explained the kind of game you would like to play with others. The idiom 'seller's market' lends an adversarial tone to your pitch, which some may find ugly. I must also wonder \u2014 when somebody says 'just for fun' in reference to a competitive selection process \u2014 if our conception of 'fun' will align in the game proper (should I stand on enough throats to win myself a place within the chronicle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T15:38:08-07:00","id":268580,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I would love to play changeling. I always seem to be the storyteller, and never a player. Any setting details?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T17:19:43-07:00","id":268634,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;I can't believe I'm doing this.&quot;<br /> <br /> Those words echoed in Dale's mind as he came up to the cliff. He gazed at how the waves below smashed against the rocks, the foam shooting up as if in protest to what he was about to do next. Looking back up at the sunset, he took a deep breath and swallowed his pride.<br /> <br /> It was ridiculous. There was no way this would work. Stuff like this only happens in fairy tales. But the trail was already cold, and it only grew colder as time went on. He spent months looking for his missing child and found no leads, except for this. He had to try everything he could, leave no stone unturned.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eiron, Eiron, Erion!&quot; he shouted to the wind. A sudden gust smacked him as if responding to his words, forcing him to turn around. And there it was.<br /> <br /> A path of briar rustled in the wind, breathing an unearthly life. The landscape changed into something completely different than the one he came from, as if he entered another world. &quot;So this must be the so-called Hedge,&quot; he deduced as he walked among the thorns. To think of the several months he spent searching, the most nonsensical lead was the only one that gave him results, as strange as they were.<br /> <br /> Then he heard his child's cries behind the briar. He wasted no time as he raced through the thorns, disregarding the pain as they cut through his flesh. It simply didn't matter to him, nothing else mattered. All that mattered right now was saving his child from whatever ungodly horrors were here. But no matter how far he ran, he didn't seem to get any closer. The cries weren't getting any louder or quieter, nor was there any response when he called his child's name over and over. He stumbled upon a clearing through the briar, and that's when things got even stranger. The cries echoed all around him now. They reverberated in and out of each other, mocking him. Tearing him at his soul as the thorns did to his body. Panic, confusion, and despair tugged at him like strings on a puppet, making him constantly swing around. Nothing made sense anymore. The cries seemed to coalesce behind him, making him turn one last time before falling to his knees.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah there you are, Dale,&quot; the creature greeted in his child's giggling voice.</i><br /> <hr /><br /> Hope that was to your liking, because I've been itching to play me some Changeling. I'm not really picky on how I play it, whether it'd be PBP, live, or a combination of the two like you were suggesting. While I have no idea how a combination of PBP and live could work, I'm eager to see what you've come up with, as it sounds pretty interesting. No matter how it's played, I too wanna tell an awesome story with others. My character, as you might have already guessed, is Dale, a Darkling detective who takes cases from both mortals and changelings alike.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1022153\" target=\"_blank\">Here's his sheet</a><br /> <br /> His background's got plenty of hooks to work with and ways to get him into various situations. Also, I'm willing to change pretty much anything around if it doesn't fit with the chronicle you have in mind(like if it doesn't take place in America, for example).<br /> <br /> As for selling myself, well for starters the sample writing above speaks for itself. Did you notice that a lot of words and phrases seem to come up exactly three times throughout the prose? Matches the same number of times Dale yelled Eiron. Coincidence? Well, I'll let you decide on that one. Also, I came up with Dale, backstory and all, in a couple days tops. Speaking of his backstory, there's also the fact that I've purposely made several things ambiguous, and not just because they're unimportant. For example, what happened to Dale's child(did you also notice the fact I completely avoided referring to them by a pronoun until now)? What of his fetch and wife? Are they still kicking? How do the authorities see this private detective, especially since he has no records whatsoever? Thing is, I know which aspects of my character to determine myself, and which to leave up to you, allowing you to organically integrate my character into your chronicle.<br /> <br /> I hope to have impressed you enough to get into this chronicle. But either way, thank you for reading this block of text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T19:32:16-07:00","id":268703,"title":"","content":"Leaper,<br /> You might be right, and I apologize if the tone threw anyone off. Reading over things, I did make a couple mistakes - I meant most of the &quot;siccing everyone at another's throats&quot; stuff as pure tongue-in-cheek humor, but that tone had no way to transmit through the medium. I actually meant &quot;just for fun&quot; to mean that folks could be humorous with the &quot;I shall prevail! I am eenweencible!&quot; stuff, since it's for fun, rather than for brownie points or anything like that.<br /> <br /> Man. I'm starting to think I might need to work on this forum posting thing. <br /> <br /> As for the sort of game I like to play, well...<br /> <br /> I like to build a world filled with things and people for the players to meet and explore, and to let the players' choices determine the direction of the action - if there's a troll blocking the bridge, the characters *can* fight him, or they can sneak around, pay the toll, or seduce the guy if they prefer. I actually tend not to prefer player-versus-player conflict as a matter of course, though when it happens I tend to monitor or moderate rather than out-and-out vetoing. The tone of the game can vary depend on the players' interests, but for Lost I generally enjoy dark adventure tinged with a mad whimsy. That said, if the majority of the players prefer Machiavellian politicking or bloody-speared conquest I try to be flexible. <br /> <br /> A'T, I haven't decided upon a final setting yet (I intend to let the group have some input) but it'll probably be set in the United States, likely in a city like Chicago or New York. I expect it'll be a fairly traditional Seasonal freehold, I traditionally enjoy starting the game in Autumn, if only for the tone of things. <br /> <br /> Carp, thanks for the post! The character looks like he could be fun. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T07:44:48-07:00","id":269026,"title":"","content":"Good to know, but I feel I won't be a proactive enough person and someone with the right amount of writing and plot-hooks you're after... I srill will love reading this as it goes along though. Hopefully I might also get the inspiration to pitch a character background once I see what more people end up doing with this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T18:50:31-07:00","id":271936,"title":"","content":"Well, it looks like I'm the only one willing at this point. However, I have found a thread where there's a few players itching for a Changeling game over at the rpg.net forums, and they just so happen to need a GM. So yeah, if you're willing to wait just a little longer for players, these guys might be interested. Here's a link to their thread: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?738474-Interest-GM-wanted-Changeling-The-Lost-or-Eberron\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...ost-or-Eberron</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T22:27:35-07:00","id":272044,"title":"","content":"Carp, <br /> I'll take a look, thanks! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T01:18:18-07:00","id":272109,"title":"","content":"I am interested! But I only heard about this game from the RPG.net thread minutes ago, so I don't have my stuff together.<br /> <br /> I did have the character fully in mind - dusting off a Darkling Mirrorskin/Nightsinger of Autumn whose game never fully manifested. Snagged on prom night after misusing a cursed tome/fae beacon, and then used for lots of identity experimentation (she is, naggingly, not 100% sure she's the original Alicia). She'd wanted to become a music teacher, and is pissed that her Fetch got to (and also became a nun). The original background details assume midtown Manhattan, New York, but I can transplant her to the affluent part of wherever.<br /> <br /> She ended up in the Autumn court, and uses her performing abilities to set the 'proper' fears back into people while trying to claw back some shards of her former life from her Fetch. She's probably headed toward The Scarecrow Ministry.<br /> <br /> Buuut that has a lot of overlap with the darkling mirrorskin of autumn detective, even though their backgrounds are very different. So I'm thinking I should probably go with something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T01:22:53-07:00","id":272112,"title":"","content":"Also, does anyone know how to subscribe to a thread on this forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T01:51:43-07:00","id":272116,"title":"","content":"Another RPG.net refugee, reportin' in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T03:52:46-07:00","id":272135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=272112#post272112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, does anyone know how to subscribe to a thread on this forum?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Subscribe button at the top of each thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T05:41:49-07:00","id":272164,"title":"","content":"Is there space for another player? I'm the one who initiated the thread on rpgnet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T09:06:15-07:00","id":272252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=272135#post272135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a Subscribe button at the top of each thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, I remembered there being one but I don't see it. I wonder if it's because I'm using Chrome now? That'd be weird.<br /> <br /> *tries something*<br /> <br /> *blinks*<br /> <br /> Huh. The Chrome version of AdBlock disabled it. Super-weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T12:22:24-07:00","id":272430,"title":"","content":"Aaaaactually I'm starting to realize I'm in too many PbPs right now as it is. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T22:23:24-07:00","id":272742,"title":"","content":"And one more rpg.net player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4000-markov","name":"Markov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:40:28-07:00","id":273054,"title":"","content":"Hello, I'm still interested! I went on a short vacation for the past two days, and simply hadn't checked since my last post. As a player, I would check much more frequently.<br /> <br /> So do you still want some fiction/character ideas? I might be able to get something down later today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T00:50:08-07:00","id":273523,"title":"","content":"Confirming that I'm still here. Full pitch incoming tomorrow, but have a short version. A med school student triggers a Key during a stupid hazing game, falls right into the clutches of the Fae and simultaneously gets replaced with a Fetch. She's tasked with &quot;fixing the broken toys&quot;, which are often hobgobliins or fellow changelings - needless to say, winning her master's favor by prolonging the suffering of her fellows doesn't sit well with her, but it was done. Some of them also escaped, mostly independent of her, and they remember.<br /> <br /> Now that she's back, I can see a lot of potential hooks. She's slipped into a &quot;not-exactly-above-board physician&quot; role. which is bound to bring her in contact with plenty of desperate, downtrodden and dangerous people. Her most long-term plan at the moment is getting a fully realized alternate identity and putting her skills to legitimate use.. She's a little fuzzy on the Fetch, and so am I, that's the fun part!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3994,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","user":"Dwyad","date":". 10-07-2014, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T17:46:44-07:00","id":274321,"title":"","content":"Hello, again, I'm back with some fiction. I felt a &quot;comic&quot; character would be fun:<br /> <br /> Mitch pulled open a draw in his desk and drew out a fifth of some dark liquor \u2013 the label had been torn off. He sat it on the desk and gestured towards it, as if to say <i>help yourself</i>. He put a cigarette in his mouth and lit it with his finger, his glazed eyes lingering on the flame just long enough to accidentally light the end of his shirt sleeve on fire.<br /> \u201cYou\u2019re, uh, on fire again,\u201d grunted the dwarf.<br /> \u201cWho is?\u201d Mitch asked.<br /> \u201cYou,\u201d the dwarf answered, much more gruffly this time. This managed to provoke a response from Mitch, who patted out the spreading flame with his other hand, cigarette clenched between his teeth, fuming smoke out of his mouth.<br /> \u201cThis was a mistake\u2026\u201d the dwarf rose.<br /> \u201cHold on dude,\u201d Mitch gestured to the chair again, \u201cI can help ya\u2019 out no problem.\u201d<br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think you are even sober, so I doubt that,\u201d he turned.<br /> Mitch cut the dwarf off physically, rushing in front of him, smoke curling around the two of them. \u201cI know I may not be\u2026 straight or stiff or whatever, but I was a great attorney before my time in faerie, and now\u2026 now I\u2019m still pretty good. I did <i>pro bono </i>cases and was assigned work by the judge and everything. I won-some-lost-some but mostly I settled things out of court and helped poor folks avoid jail time for being poor. You\u2019re facing jail time here pal, I don\u2019t care what fancy tricks you brought back from Arcadia, there is just no use getting your <i>also known as</i> mired in legal troubles and have to break free or go on the run or get a whole new identify.\u201d<br /> \u201cWhat would you do for me\u2026\u201d the dwarf\u2019s eyes betrayed his desire.<br /> \u201cI can get you off this no trouble\u2026 my secret though. Your case vanishes and then the harassment stops from the pigs stop. You can get back to your gardening.\u201d<br /> \u201cBut what do you get out of it? You weren\u2019t forced to represent me.\u201d<br /> \u201cEasy \u2013 you gotta grow me something in that patch \u2018o yours through the hedge. Don\u2019t worry about it, I\u2019ll be in touch.\u201d<br /> \u201cHow can you be in this place and not burn it down by mistake? You are careless! And put that damn cigarette out \u2013 aren\u2019t there smoke detectors in here!?\u201d<br /> Mitch smiled a slow half grin, \u201clisten shorty, nobody cares about what goes on in the PD office. My clients are prostitutes and burglars who are too poor to afford an attorney. The public doesn\u2019t care if they get a fair trial or not \u2013 <i>nobody checks in here or gives a damn whether I do my job or not</i>. Plus, I took out the smoke detectors when I got back \u2013 didn\u2019t suit my \u2018temperament\u2019 anymore.\u201d<br /> There was a sudden ringing before the sprinklers turned on, dousing the two of them with gallons of water.<br /> \u201cGuess I missed one\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> So my inspiration here was to play a fire/trickster spirit. I see Mitch as a spring courtier who has decided to just relax and not care too much about the consequences of his actions. He was passionate and he was good at his job before he was taken, but now that he is back he has decided to lay low, enjoy life, and stay comfy. Not too much else has been fleshed out. As a character, he would add some interesting hooks, make mistakes (the best kinds, of course) and keep others on their toes.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T21:53:17-07:00","id":274493,"title":"","content":"All right! Thanks for the renewed interest! <br /> <br /> To make sure everyone gets a chance to post, I'll extend things 'til this Friday. I'll post then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T14:18:25-07:00","id":275735,"title":"","content":"cool, looking forward to it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T04:07:32-07:00","id":276163,"title":"","content":"I'll be playing a Wizened character. An inventor/accountant for the group. A jack of all trades with a dark side very close to the goblins of lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:11:39-07:00","id":276373,"title":"","content":"What the heck, I'll post here, could use some recreational writing.<br /> <br /> ************************************************** *********************************<br /> <br /> &quot;It came upon a midnight clear with an old glorious song by beings like angels bending near the earth, but they weren't. I don't remember how they came to me, all I could see was that colour streaming down out from the space above and I couldn't find the will to move as a solid shape formed and I saw my own face flow down over the stardust and shadow stepping past me with a blank expression. Or maybe I was walking past it. Maybe neither of us were moving, but space between us shifted and shrunk. I don't know. But then I was in the light and It was in the fields below. It went on to live with my husband and raise my child. While I remained in that light and pulled up (or was it down) into that brilliant night.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't say what they were. They were Vorlons and Shadows, they were the Drej, they were the Greys and the Body Snatchers. Silence and Daleks and Weeping Angels. They were things I couldn't really understand at all. I don't think they changed and when they seemed different then I never noticed, or felt it was only because I was realizing something new about them, but something which had only recently come to my attention.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't remember all that happened in that place, or was it places, it felt like hours (and sometimes days), but when I finally took a left turn where I was told to go right, it was sixty years ahead. The daze cleared and my mind returned. I can't say I escaped. All I did was get distracted a moment and take a wrong turn and suddenly I was back here. My husband dead, that thing masquerading still as me and my child a grandparent of his own. I may just be another experiment being run. Or maybe the entire thing was an experiment, trying to see how long it would be before I found the way out of the maze and returned to the human world. Maybe they've finished with me. Or maybe they haven't.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I've studied since then. They appeared like creatures out of the science fiction of your history. Maybe they saw that coming, maybe they're the future and took a trip to the past. That place(s?) only made sense while I was still there, maybe time works differently? But maybe they influenced these things. Anyway, I study, I learn to reach out from my place here using these computers. I'd say they were primitive, by they aren't. What They had weren't computers. They had buttons and displays and processes, but they weren't computers. They were an image of computers, like something a child makes to play pretend with. But still, these work the same way, functionally if not mechanically. And they let me interact with the world without needing to meet it face to face.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;One thing is certain, They are still here. They still take people. And they still take us back to that place when they can find us, so I learn what I can of them and I hide where they can't find me. And if I keep doing this, maybe, eventually, I might find a way to do more.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Free, aka Meaghan Scully, was taken in 1946 from the ranch her and her husband owned in Colorado. She finally returned 2006.<br /> <br /> Her fae seeming is that of a woman with what on first glance seems to be shiny black hair, but a closer look reveals to be a starfield complete with constellations. The stars remain still as she moves and so the hair seems to map out a sky...not Earth's sky, but a sky. Her eyes are much too large and violet with no visible pupils. Her eyebrows are bald, stealing away some of her facial expressiveness and giving her a blank, staring sort of countenance. Little sparks of electricity dance across the empty air between her fingers. The air always seems to be moving just the slightest bit towards her. Her nails appear to be black, but really aren't there at all. Instead it is a simple blackness over the tops of her fingers and toes as if there were a hole there despite the feel of a finger's nail. Her skin and body seems to have a curious give to it, as if it were filled with nothing but air, or maybe not even that, and surrounded by a resilient, sensitive shell of slick rubber-like flesh. Maybe...maybe the skin of her fae seeming is yet just another container, like her Mask, something to keep the burgeoning truth of what she is(will be) hidden within.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why will I make it? I have actual art of the character (not the best since the artist didn't understand what I was asking for by his own admission, but still actual art) and because she was touched by Vorlons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://fav.me/d6iacd5\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/0a81120e-55f9-4931-9660-a5dc9d4f9964/d6iacd5-0847c5dc-b9a4-4445-a10f-8cd215617be9.png/v1/fill/w_900,h_670/free_changeling_nwod_character_by_thrythlind_d6iacd5-fullview.png?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..HksFWhNGaTUD9O5HKk44JIratGAwq0UOl52LCru7eiM\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fav.me/d6iacd5\" target=\"_blank\"> Free - Changeling NWoD Character by Thrythlind on DeviantArt </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fav.me/d6iacd5\" target=\"_blank\"> http://fav.me/d6iacd5 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Free - Changeling NWoD Character &mdash; artwork by Thrythlind on DeviantArt. Published: 2013-08-15 &middot; Likes: 21 &middot; Views: 1069 &middot; Comments: 4 </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-10-2014, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T01:06:33-07:00","id":277048,"title":"","content":"&quot;Another one? Really?&quot; Malory didn't say it, but she was thinking it loudly enough you could read it off her eyes, this is the twenty-sixth one this month. A man, vaguely Hispanic, wearing blue-on-black with a new coat of red, courtesy of three shotgun pellets to the right shoulder. She learned a long time ago to not to ask why, it made life a little easier - people with good reasons don't end up laid out on stolen workbenches in abandoned warehouses.<br /> <br /> If she were anyone else, that arm would never work again. If she were anyone else, that man would have to retire from a life of petty violence. If she were anyone else, he'd probably end up sadder but wiser, his life longer but poorer. She is, unfortunately, just that damn good.<br /> <br /> Wire hangers heated over a lighter, a long shard of glass, a spool of fishing line, and a heavy dose of heroin, these are the things back-alley miracles are made of.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dios mio..&quot; Patient #26 muttered through the opiate haze.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hon, he's got nothin' to do with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Have a doktor! <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1029662\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...heetid=1029662</a><br /> <br /> In her Fae Mien, she looks like a stitched together ghoul-girl, pale skin and catgut scars. To the Mask, the scars turn to early wrinkles, and a nigh-literal skeletal figure with linen-white skin turns to a sickly, anorexic-looking woman. She'd be mistaken for a meth addict, given her usual surroundings, were it not for the fact that her teeth are always uncannily perfect.<br /> <br /> Why will I make it, when many others won't?<br /> <br /> Because I'm your white mage, and nobody, fucks, with the white mage.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.mangauk.com/gallery/albums/album-146/lg/dbz_dende01.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3994,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","user":"Dwyad","date":". 10-10-2014, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T10:18:56-07:00","id":277340,"title":"","content":"Background/writing sample coming tonight. Just wanted to get my character sheet up, and show I was still interested in playing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1031740\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...heetid=1031740</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4000-markov","name":"Markov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:05:27-07:00","id":277465,"title":"","content":"Oh, we need a character sheet? I was going to wait for specific things like XP and such before working on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T14:05:22-07:00","id":277551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwyad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=277048#post277048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why will I make it, when many others won't?<br /> <br /> Because I'm your white mage, and nobody, fucks, with the white mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You deserve an internet for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=277465#post277465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, we need a character sheet? I was going to wait for specific things like XP and such before working on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the ST didn't say that we <i>needed</i> a character sheet, I just thought it was a good idea to make one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T22:54:55-07:00","id":277902,"title":"","content":"Okay! It's a bit after Friday, but I haven't gone to sleep yet, so it's still the same day to me! <br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone who expressed interest! My cast of players will be:<br /> <br /> Crapcarp,<br /> Thrythlind,<br /> Dwyad,<br /> and A Twannabe!<br /> <br /> You don't have to have chosen a character yet - I figured we'd work out setting and playstyle together before we set out characters, and it might be useful to have the flexibility to shift concepts if needed. <br /> <br /> So! My four players: What sort of game are you looking for? Machiavellian politics? Brutal war? Deep enigmas and occult investigation? Are there any themes you'd like to cover? <br /> <br /> When left to my own devices I usually lean toward investigation and action, though I'm willing to go in another direction if that's what the group prefers. My standard tone for Lost is darkly comic, with an edge of desperation. As for setting, I'm thinking probably a medium-to-large freehold in Chicago (though if you guys have ideas for an evocative location you'd prefer, I'm glad to consider it!). <br /> <br /> Basically, I like to let the players have a hand in building the game's world, just a bit. We'll all be playing in the sandbox, after all! If you have a fun idea for a setpiece, location, NPC, or potential conflict down the line, let me know. Maybe I can work it in!<br /> <br /> Characters will be base creation + 20 XP. Dropping Clarity for XP is allowed at 5 XP per drop, but only up to two times. If you choose to do so, we'll roll for derangements. <br /> <br /> I *love* characters to have backstories - especially ones that are rich in setting details, character establishment, and plot seeds to mine. Submitting a background with your character will be worth a minimum of 5 XP, up to 10 XP for an exceptional one. Exceptional, in this case, involves quality, rather than quantity. If your one paragraph gives me more to play with and is better-written than another guy's novel, you'll get more XP from it. If you don't feel up to writing a narrative, I can accept timelines or bullet points, too, as long as they're easy to read and get the important bits across.<br /> <br /> If anyone needs help building or fleshing out their sheet, I'm happy to do so - and I'm also glad to look over a sheet post-creation for XP efficiency, if you like, so you can have all the Cool Stuff you can afford.<br /> <br /> Regarding house rules, we're using a 2 dot in-seeming/3 dot out-of-seeming merit for Dual Kith. I'm afraid that I'm not incorporating Talecrafting into the game, as the addiction rules can just be too disruptive in play. The first dot of Court Mantle for any of the Seasonal Courts is free, though the rest cost as usual. If there's any homebrewed material you want to use, let me look it over first. I might allow it, I might allow a modified version, or I might deny it, depending on balance and suitability.<br /> <br /> I don't require training time or anything like that, but I generally prefer that XP spends in game make some sense - if you've been spending the last six months straight in Autumn's occult archives trying to find the meaning of that strange symbol that's appearing everywhere, you'll have to come up with some justification on how you've been training to boost Strength. I'm usually more lenient on lower levels than on higher ones.<br /> <br /> A note for my ST style: I take a two-tiered path when it comes to ST Veto. The first time I say &quot;no,&quot; to an idea or request, it means &quot;not at first blush, but please lay out your arguments for why I should say yes.&quot; The second time I say &quot;no,&quot; it means &quot;Not now and probably not ever, but if that changes I'll let you know.&quot; I'd rather not hit a third time, if we can avoid it.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's more than one thing I'm forgetting, so ask any questions you have! Also, let me know if you'd rather play on these forums or on a Google Doc. I'm *leaning* toward Google Doc as I don't have access to these forums at work, but I'd rather not force it if folks can't use that. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T01:10:33-07:00","id":277973,"title":"","content":"I have been without sleep for nigh unto two days, so I haven't the energy to reply to all of this, just mind that my backstory is in my sheet.<br /> <br /> Also, gotta say, the word &quot;investigation&quot;, where it intersects with &quot;PbP&quot; makes me twitchy. It has, in my experience, translated to &quot;doing nothing for days&quot;. Though I suppose we DO have a dedicated detective, Malory can try forensics, and..Yeah, like everything else, it's all in how the GM pulls it off.<br /> <br /> Also, none of those houserules are houserules, - dual Kith, at best, is an optional thing, but fully detailed in the books.<br /> <br /> And..PbP by doc seems somehow even clunkier than normal PbP. Does that work? How?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3994,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","user":"Dwyad","date":". 10-11-2014, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T07:07:15-07:00","id":278105,"title":"","content":"Everybody can contribute to the document, basically.<br /> <br /> As for me, I like redemption and recovery stories. I tend to like to see my characters start as broken in someway with the game or story one of them getting progressively better and more accepting of themselves and/or whatever caused them to be broken in the first place (accepting or defiant, depending). I also prefer Dark is Not Evil, Holy Dark, Good is Not Nice and other such concepts. I have never played an evil character, generally don't feel comfortable with it, but I have played many characters whose morality is far more old world than modern world, which many people would think is the same thing as psychopathic or evil. I also like &quot;Earn your happy ending&quot;, rather than &quot;always a happy ending.&quot;<br /> <br /> Though I suppose any &quot;happy ending&quot; in WoD would have to be earned through blood and sweat and tears...and that's fine with me.<br /> <br /> There was a dual-kith combo I used to make Free, trying to remember what it was...I don't have all the books...it was some combo of electromagnetism and cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-11-2014, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T14:48:52-07:00","id":278376,"title":"","content":"Levinquick and Snowskin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T16:03:10-07:00","id":278437,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was probably it, I'll look a bit closer later...dealing with the tail end of Virtuacon right now...one more game and one more event to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T21:49:58-07:00","id":278581,"title":"","content":"Reporting in!<br /> <br /> Just to pick some nits? It's a good thing we've got some XP, 'cause we've got a WW2 vet detective that entirely lacks combat skills. Also, Dale oughta pick up a 1911 - it's one of the few things that hasn't appreciably changed since The Good Ol' Days, and that's probably comforting. Also, look into the Scarecrow Ministry - they probably want you.<br /> <br /> As to Malory herself? I keep coming back to &quot;what about her Fetch?&quot; The reason she's Envious is because she feels fucking robbed - she did everything right, she lived a good life, she kept her nose in the book and, more or less, she genuinely wanted to help people - then she lost absolutely everything because she did the wrong nonsensical bullshit at the wrong time. If you knew what she'd been through, you wouldn't blame her for taking a bit more where she can.<br /> <br /> But what about her Fetch? It wholeheartedly believes its her, it wants to help people, and though it totally lacks the improvisational skills to be a great doctor, it's got the rote understanding down, and that's enough to be a passable one. Is it right to destroy the thing, when it's just as much a hapless victim as she was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T02:03:36-07:00","id":278681,"title":"","content":"For experience, are we using the GMC flat-experience costs or the original scaling experience costs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T02:26:09-07:00","id":278687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=266793#post266793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This will not be using GMC - I haven't had an opportunity to internalize the changes from base WoD and the game hasn't been transitioned over anyway. I haven't decided on any houserules, though any choices (such as dual-kithing with a Shadowsoul) might be subject to ST veto if I think they'll be bad for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third post in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T02:43:08-07:00","id":278690,"title":"","content":"Ah aha. I haven't parsed the abbreviations yet. Also, curious, what is wrong with dual-kithing a Shadowsoul?<br /> <br /> Also, I think it was Fireheart (the description says it includes the idea of Lightning in its concept) and Snowskin that I did before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-12-2014, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T14:17:08-07:00","id":279068,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> Glad to hear the news - looking forward to this. As far as my preferred game play, I love a good mix - political scenes and investigations, with the occasional action sequence. For me, I love it when the horror is just beneath the surface, ready to be revealed, if the characters can just scratch hard enough.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely married to the character I fleshed out earlier - but I'll start drafting a sheet and see how it goes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T18:14:15-07:00","id":279247,"title":"","content":"You'll have to ask the GM to be sure, but Shadowsouls get quite a lot of bennies for nothing. +Wyrd to intimidation, 9-again subterfuge and an Affinity. None of this costs Glamour. That means they're pretty much better than Snowskins at the things Snowskins are supposed to be good at. Plus they nick Darkness, which is one of only two Contracts Darklings get.<br /> <br /> If that's your only trick, it's a bit much, but if you dual-kith it, things can get a little over-the-top right quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T18:15:29-07:00","id":279252,"title":"","content":"The issue with the Shadowsoul is that it gets 3 kith benefits, where most get one or two at most. In addition, several of those benefits are more powerful than other kiths' entire benefit, let alone singular powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T21:13:35-07:00","id":279368,"title":"","content":"I am looking at the following concepts<br /> <br /> Free - Touched by the Vorlons - Winter hacker, elemental - Info-gathering/elemental stuff<br /> Heigou - Black Dog - Summer or Autumn hidden defender of the innocent and tormentor of evil, darkling - Stealth/Combat<br /> Akaboshi - Nightclub Dominatrix - A spring ogre with a trace of succubus or something similar - Social/combat<br /> Random - Creature Feature - a reptilian beasst who works at a vintage movie theater, Spring - combat/hollow<br /> <br /> other than that we have a doctor and a detective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-13-2014, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T21:16:32-07:00","id":280546,"title":"","content":"wrong place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T21:17:22-07:00","id":280547,"title":"","content":"Since there was no commentary, I'll just go with my original thought and use Free.<br /> <br /> Meaghan Scully was born in Chicago during the roaring twenties, the child of factory worker and a waitress. She group during the unfortunate period now know as the Great Depression and wasn't much different from any other young girl at the time. She certainly wasn't the type that was at all interested in the sciences or anything like that. She was quite a bit more down to Earth and centered in the day to day worries of helping her family get enough to eat by doing sewing, laundry and other small jobs for other people in her neighborhood, those that could afford to pay for a little extra help, that is. When she reached high school, she started working as a waitress similar to her mother. Then came Roosevelt and the New Deal producing jobs for all sorts of people that had before been jobless. With her siblings mostly grown into adults and their own lives and her parents being taken care of by the new Social Security measures, she wasn't needed as much any longer, but had already found it hard to break the habits she had developed in that time. She was already focused on doing work.<br /> <br /> In the 1930s, Meaghan a young mechanic's apprentice with a slight hispanic look and a Texan drawl came into her restaurant and started to flirt with her. He hadn't been the first, but she responded with her usual polite dismissal and focusing on business rather than acknowledging the attempt. Strangely enough, the young man wasn't dissuaded and persisted in his efforts, regaling her with his intentions to earn enough money to buy his own ranch, until she finally gave in and began to date him. They were married in late 1938, Meaghan taking his name Reyes, and had a son in 1940 as the world started to descend into war around them. When the Japanese attacked Pearl Harbor and the call went out for volunteers, her husband, Jacob, answered and joined up, even volunteering for the paratroopers. For most of four years, Meaghan raised her son Martin on her own, fretting over the stories of the war, trying to keep calm through the Siege of Bastogne and doing everything she could to save the money that Jacob sent home to her. Finally he returned home...and he'd returned home with a windfall that Meaghan was never able to learn the source of. Between the money that she had saved during the war, her waitressing and his combat pay, and the money that he had brought home with him, they had enough to purchase some fallow land in Colorado and start that ranch that Jacob wanted.<br /> <br /> Things should have gone on from there as happily as any fairy tale. Unfortunately, They came for her in 1946. Alien abductions would not receive widespread attention and enter into the framework of American folklore for at least another eleven years when Antonio Vilas Boas claimed to have been abducted and returned, or four years after that when Betty and Barney Hill would make a similar claim. Meaghan was gone before those things ever happened.<br /> <br /> ************************************************** ************<br /> (reprint of earlier bit in Meaghan's words)<br /> <br /> &quot;It came upon a midnight clear with an old glorious song by beings like angels bending near the earth, but they weren't. I don't remember how they came to me, all I could see was that colour streaming down out from the space above and I couldn't find the will to move as a solid shape formed and I saw my own face flow down over the stardust and shadow stepping past me with a blank expression. Or maybe I was walking past it. Maybe neither of us were moving, but space between us shifted and shrunk. I don't know. But then I was in the light and It was in the fields below. It went on to live with my husband and raise my child. While I remained in that light and pulled up (or was it down) into that brilliant night.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't say what they were. They were Vorlons and Shadows, they were the Drej, they were the Greys and the Body Snatchers. Silence and Daleks and Weeping Angels. They were things I couldn't really understand at all. I don't think they changed and when they seemed different then I never noticed, or felt it was only because I was realizing something new about them, but something which had only recently come to my attention.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't remember all that happened in that place, or was it places, it felt like hours (and sometimes days), but when I finally took a left turn where I was told to go right, it was sixty years ahead. The daze cleared and my mind returned. I can't say I escaped. All I did was get distracted a moment and take a wrong turn and suddenly I was back here. My husband dead, that thing masquerading still as me and my child a grandparent of his own. I may just be another experiment being run. Or maybe the entire thing was an experiment, trying to see how long it would be before I found the way out of the maze and returned to the human world. Maybe they've finished with me. Or maybe they haven't.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I've studied since then. They appeared like creatures out of the science fiction of your history. Maybe they saw that coming, maybe they're the future and took a trip to the past. That place(s?) only made sense while I was still there, maybe time works differently? But maybe they influenced these things. Anyway, I study, I learn to reach out from my place here using these computers. I'd say they were primitive, by they aren't. What They had weren't computers. They had buttons and displays and processes, but they weren't computers. They were an image of computers, like something a child makes to play pretend with. But still, these work the same way, functionally if not mechanically. And they let me interact with the world without needing to meet it face to face.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;One thing is certain, They are still here. They still take people. And they still take us back to that place when they can find us, so I learn what I can of them and I hide where they can't find me. And if I keep doing this, maybe, eventually, I might find a way to do more.&quot;<br /> <br /> ************************************************** **********<br /> <br /> When Meaghan returned in 2008, she took a long while to find a place for herself. She had peeked in on her Fetch, looking like a woman in her late 80s, but moving with surprising health and vigor. Her son was married and had his own family, even his children had mostly already married and moved on to form there own families. The ranch had been very successful and the little house Meaghan remembered had been replaced by something akin to a mansion. The family had interests in other businesses now, though she wasn't sure where all that money had come from. Jacob Reyes had died some years before, so she assumed she'd never find the answer to why he'd gained such great financial luck. The family had kept a military tradition as well, though given their wealth they were more often officers than grunt soldiers. Her own son had spent some time in Vietnam and one of her grand-daughters had become a career Air Force meterologist.<br /> <br /> Uncertain of what to do and unable to get her old life back, it no longer seemed to exist, she instead slunk into hiding and considered her captors. Returning to her maiden name and taking the nickname of &quot;Free&quot; among other changelings. Meaghan has spent a lot of time studying science as well as the history of alien abductions as well as faerie related disappearances. She prowls the internet message boards where conspiracy theorists gather and take in the stories, trying to separate dross from gold. She is convinced that her science fiction seeming captors had set up the scenario and the experiment with the purpose of trying to understand the concepts of science and the like. She thinks that such scientific knowledge could be tapped in the same way that the concept of the seasons were tapped. Invoking or making deals with some concept or entity alien to the Gentry and using that to further conceal the changelings from their old masters. Some part of her also wonders if such things could be made into a weapon as well.<br /> <br /> When possible, Free prefers to interact over chat-rooms and the like. Even with her Mask, she is aware that her voice is disturbing to other people and likes to avoid having that reminder that she is no longer human pushed into her face. She walks a fine line between purpose and obsession; solitude and isolation.<br /> <br /> She does have one past-time that is not directly related to her changeling nature or her research into the Others. Free has become a major science-fiction fan and even maintains a blog and forums titled &quot;Touched by Vorlons&quot; which discusses science-fiction and fantasy stories.<br /> <br /> ************************************************** *****************<br /> <br /> The character sheet is at home, I need to make a couple of changes and haven't spent XP yet, not that I expect that to affect much. I thought about giving her a Hollow, but that is prohibitively expensive in the original experience point costs framework. She will likely have some mortal resources and status instead. Any bonus xp for the above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-14-2014, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T21:33:56-07:00","id":280558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=277902#post277902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! My four players: What sort of game are you looking for? Machiavellian politics? Brutal war? Deep enigmas and occult investigation? Are there any themes you'd like to cover?<br /> <br /> When left to my own devices I usually lean toward investigation and action, though I'm willing to go in another direction if that's what the group prefers. My standard tone for Lost is darkly comic, with an edge of desperation. As for setting, I'm thinking probably a medium-to-large freehold in Chicago (though if you guys have ideas for an evocative location you'd prefer, I'm glad to consider it!).<br /> <br /> Basically, I like to let the players have a hand in building the game's world, just a bit. We'll all be playing in the sandbox, after all! If you have a fun idea for a setpiece, location, NPC, or potential conflict down the line, let me know. Maybe I can work it in!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not too awfully picky about the themes and moods, so long as it's unmistakably Changeling. Though if I was pressed to pick something, I'd say maybe going for the aforementioned investigation and action with a dash of noir. But maybe that's just because of Dale. But also for a little something else.<br /> <br /> See, I'm also in a group called Cardians, it's a custom Hunter conspiracy and there are several different cells of players called divisions. In my case, I'm in the Abroad division(we go everywhere in the world), but there's another division starting up called Cardians: Chicago, and that will apparently have a detective noir tone to it(or so I've heard). So yeah, while I'm not suggesting full-on crossover or anything, it's just a little something to think about for the world of this chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=277902#post277902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure there's more than one thing I'm forgetting, so ask any questions you have! Also, let me know if you'd rather play on these forums or on a Google Doc. I'm *leaning* toward Google Doc as I don't have access to these forums at work, but I'd rather not force it if folks can't use that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't mind if we go Google Doc. Hell, I've done it before, so it shouldn't be too hard. Just a few organizational rules here and there and we should be sweet. Though it looks like some peeps wanna do it the traditional way. Either way, I'm fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T21:41:40-07:00","id":280576,"title":"","content":"I am also fine with google doc we just need to avoid the urge to edit earlier portions of the doc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T16:51:24-07:00","id":281636,"title":"","content":"Hey guys.<br /> <br /> I don't think Mitch fits too well - too much of a 'comic' vibe. I noticed we were a little focused on mental skills and capabilities and thought it would be fun to incorporate a more &quot;brute&quot; strength into the mix. Here is the background for my idea. Tell me what you think:<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> &quot;The scars on my chest are from dad, dear old. Took a knife to me and mom, but I managed to survive. I didn\u2019t spend too much longer around Chicago before I joined up. I always liked working on cars so I got to work with the engine - got my degree and everything. Of course, I made some side money fighting in the ring. Never thought I\u2019d be proud of something but my time boxing made me happy.<br /> <br /> Of course, we got to float all over. I\u2019ve been to Japan, Korea, India\u2026 all over Asia. It\u2019s different there. Girls are the same though. Or at least their disease was. Took a bottle to the head in Malaysia, that\u2019s what this bump on my head is.<br /> <br /> I was fading, getting past my prime when the deal maker came. He didn\u2019t look like the devil, didn\u2019t act like him either. I\u2019m certain there isn\u2019t any devil other than myself though, just so we\u2019re clear. I was shipping home, and I figured I could become a boxer and become the heavyweight champion. This guy says he\u2019s a captain of a private boat, and needs a little help with the engine. He said he pay me in training \u2013 had some champions under his employ in the past, all I had to do was sign up for 2 years\u2019 service. I took the deal, and he dragged me through those thorns, sharper than dad\u2019s knife.<br /> <br /> There was a bay, with a boat, and a captain, but there wasn\u2019t much else. Captain said there was treasure in the boat, but I never saw any. He chained me to the boat, which was sunk under the water, and told me not to let anything in or out of the boat. At low tide, there was just enough length on the chain for me to put my nose above the surface and breathe, but after high tide I learned to hold my breath.<br /> <br /> Sharks came. Squid came. Men came. Creatures came. I choked them. I smashed their skulls. I strangled them with my irons. My skin tore so much it healed back like scales. I swam so much these webs came up between my fingers. I held my breath so long, I don\u2019t miss the oxygen that much. But those chains scarred my leg \u2013 you can still see the ring around my ankle.<br /> <br /> He held his word though, the Captain. Brought me back and left me somewhere in the middle of the pacific. I guess he thought I would die, but I was picked up by some freighter, and landed in San Fran. I didn\u2019t know where else to go so I hitched back to Chicago. Now the city pays me to work the bridges. I guess its fine work.&quot;<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> Freddy has endured the life of the brutally abused, and has not been afraid to pay back in kind. He is not cruel, or evil, but in his own estimation, he is fair, maybe even level headed, regardless of what others say.<br /> <br /> His time in the Navy helped him get him training in engine and mechanical work, skills he is still proud of. It also gave him a place to vent his physical prowess in the boxing ring, both sanctioned and sub rosa.<br /> <br /> His durance under the Captain warped him into the monster of the deeps he is today. He is still drawn to the water, and likes to be near it, but knows that terrible things, even worse than him live down deep.<br /> <br /> Upon his return to Chicago, he never really tried to reclaim his old life \u2013 there wasn\u2019t much to claim anyway. He fell in with the winter court because it just made sense to him. There is sorrow in this life, and he has seen it and felt it.<br /> <br /> His whole life he has held onto the memory of his mother, lost to him. He sees her in his dreams sometimes, and it was her memory that he thinks preserved his mind amidst all those bloody tides. He is not meditative, and he is not crazy, but in moments of stress and panic he finds himself retreating mentally to his memories with her. Afterwards, he drowns in his emotions of missing her, and the life he thinks was robbed of him \u2013 not by his keeper, but by his dad. Dad did some time in prison, but Freddy has no idea what became of him. He just assumes he is out there somewhere. If he meets him, he\u2019ll drive a knife into his skull. But he doesn\u2019t think that dream will ever come true.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> So, there are my two ideas. Mitch, the burnout public defender, and Freddy, the brutal bridge troll. Any thoughts? I'm leaning towards the bridge troll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T20:25:23-07:00","id":281874,"title":"","content":"Frankly, either one could work. If you'd rather go bridge troll, that's fine for me. <br /> <br /> So! We have a Spring Court back-alley doc, a Winter Court bridge troll, an obsessive Autumn detective, and another Winter Court hacker/dataminer, eh? That gives me some ideas.<br /> <br /> As for the backgrounds I've seen so far: Freddy, Meghan, and Malory each get 7 XP. Carp, will you be writing any more for Dale, or leaving his background as is?<br /> <br /> Oh, and there will be no Orwellian revision of the Google Doc unless the whole group agrees to retcon something. That's ground we don't want to travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T04:12:40-07:00","id":282151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=281874#post281874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carp, will you be writing any more for Dale, or leaving his background as is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I've made a few little tweaks here and there to Dale's character. For starters, considering what Dwyad said about about Dale being in the Scarecrow Ministry, I've taken their advice and done it. Problem was that my character didn't fit the prerequisites, so I made a few changes to compensate. For starters, I put the third dot that was originally in Dale's Composure and put it in his Manipulation. After that, I used up 6 of the initial Merit dots to boost up his Wyrd to 3, which left one more dot for the Autumn Mantle. Then I used 10 XP to bring up the Mantle to 3 dots, and 6 XP to get 2 dots in Harvest. After that, I used the 4 remaining XP for 1 dot in the Dream Contract. And now that he's met the Entitlement's prerequisites, he now has the Bugbear's Mask token.<br /> <br /> As for Dale's backstory, it's pretty much the same, but I've added a little extra to include the whole Scarecrow Ministry thing. You can read the entire thing on the sheet itself, but here's the update in and of itself:<br /> <br /> <i>Inevitably, he comes across people who get a little too nosy about the world behind the veil, usually his mortal clients or mortals who are just nosy by nature. He takes care of these people by scaring them witless, which grants him a steady supply of Glamour. But the main reason he does it is to keep them away from that veil. Afterall, when he looked behind it, he was dragged into Hell itself. This activity attracted the Scarecrow Ministry's attention, and they happily accepted him after he succeeded their tests with flying colors. Now, he's developed an urban legend of his own devising around Chicago.<br /> <br /> It is said a killer stalks the streets at night. His name is Sullivan the Seeker. He targets those with curiosity on their minds, because he's a curious fellow himself, and like attracts like. Nobody knows what exactly he's seeking, but there are a few theories floating about. Some say he's looking for the hairy, mushy, shriveled-up mess that is his heart, and thinks it's beating in someone's chest. Others say he's looking for the perfect nightmare, and thinks you have to gnaw it out the brain of the one who experienced it. Still others say he's looking for himself, but since he died long ago, he never will, so he simply delivers the same fate he suffered out of revenge to fate itself. The police never manage to catch him because he can melt into the darkness. He is the darkness.<br /> <br /> He doesn't do any killing, though. The point is the spread fear to keep the mortals in line, not to kill them. However, he knows that if blood isn't spilled soon, Sullivan will lose his fangs...</i><br /> <br /> Other than that, his backstory is unchanged. <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1022153\" target=\"_blank\">Here's his sheet again, for convenience.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T04:32:43-07:00","id":282158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This will not be using GMC - I haven't had an opportunity to internalize the changes from base WoD and the game hasn't been transitioned over anyway. I haven't decided on any houserules, though any choices (such as dual-kithing with a Shadowsoul) might be subject to ST veto if I think they'll be bad for the game. </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping to run a chronicle or participate in one once Changeling 2ed becomes a finished thing. If anyone here is on board with running Changeling 2ed in either post-by-post or Roll20 format, I will announce it, but so far I'm looking for players among Skype contacts. And good luck running your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T05:55:02-07:00","id":282186,"title":"","content":"Okay, Free's sheet is here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1035366\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...heetid=1035366</a><br /> <br /> Her status and contacts are all online and she hasn't met any of them face to face. She has a bit more awareness of human hunters due to her online investigations in situations and event analysis and participation on certain boards.<br /> <br /> Her Fringe Events specialty is based on her tracing anomalous patterns in events other people consider unimportant or hoaxes. Her resources are from online businesses, such as movie/gaming reviews and such.<br /> <br /> Vacuums are still used in a lot of technology ranging from door seals to light bulbs. So the control elements can be useful...not sure about the first level...but maybe heavy, sucking wind storms like tornadoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-15-2014, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T19:13:35-07:00","id":283061,"title":"","content":"I'm iffy on Contracts of Elements: Vacuum. Elements specifically refers to substances, tangible things. Vacuum is... sort of the opposite, really.<br /> <br /> Carp, 8 XP total for your background. <br /> <br /> I'm liking those Mythweaver sheets, if you can put one together, A'T. <br /> <br /> Can folks put up an XP Log in the Statistics Block field, to help keep track of that stuff? Something like: <br /> <br /> Resources 1 (2 XP)<br /> Resources 2 (4 XP) <br /> Fang &amp; Talon 4 (16 XP)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 10-15-2014, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T19:18:53-07:00","id":283088,"title":"","content":"I could switch it to air then. Vacuum can be a derivation of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-16-2014, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T22:24:54-07:00","id":283322,"title":"","content":"That I'd be okay with, in theory, though I should warn you that creating a vacuum with Elements: Air 3 won't be an incredibly easy prospect, and maintaining one will take even more effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T02:04:44-07:00","id":283632,"title":"","content":"I figure the mechanics would just be the same as air and would be written as air, with the contract being something of the idea of her envisioning little bits of vacuum here and there to pull the air this way or that...entirely fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:42:08-07:00","id":284295,"title":"","content":"Hey y'all. I made an account at myth weavers, and I started editing a sheet, but when I clicked &quot;save changes&quot; it said I couldn't edit the sheet... I think I missed a crucial step in the process. Can anyone help me out? Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T16:06:34-07:00","id":284310,"title":"","content":"Myth weavers has an incredibly short memory. <br /> <br /> When you sign in you can click &quot;remember me&quot; so that it puts a cookie on your system. If you don't want to have autolog info on your comp, you can instead open a second tab, do not close the one you are working on, and relog into your account. Then go back to your working tab and save. I had to do this with Free's sheet because I forgot to click Remember Me when I logged in. <br /> <br /> <br /> In other comments, I'd be vaguely amused if two of Free's online contacts were &quot;Binary Hex&quot;, &quot;Little Sister&quot; and &quot;Waffles&quot; just for reference bits. <br /> <br /> Binary Hex is a hacker in the Knights of the Night podcast's WoD:Hunter game. We don't know much about him/her/it yet. <br /> <br /> Little Sister was an AI from my brother's superhero setting: United. Grew out of a device meant to take complete control of attached security systems. (Little Sister Pwns Big Brother). Of course, would just be a screen name in WoD. <br /> <br /> Waffles is the hacker name for one of the characters in a scion game of mine. Daughter of Lugh, reincarnated Galahad. Who once defeated an army of 500 skilled mortal hackers led by a legendary mortal and assisted by two other scion hackers. (To be fair, the army had other concerns and they didn't put full focus on her right away. The bad guys were assaulting Seattle at the time and the hacker army was part of it.)<br /> <br /> Don't need it at all, Waffles and Little Sister certainly don't fit NWoD. But the thought just came to me today and I was amused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T16:21:20-07:00","id":284314,"title":"","content":"Wow, you are not kidding. Thanks, Solved the problem.<br /> <br /> Voila: <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1036354\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...heetid=1036354</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T16:59:00-07:00","id":284349,"title":"","content":"No problem. <br /> <br /> Also just noticed the XP log request. Will add that when I get home later. Today is looking to be a short day at work so will have time between end of classes and my Swords in the Mist game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T04:57:42-07:00","id":284852,"title":"","content":"Groovy! <br /> <br /> Sorry I've been a bit patchy lately - been an incredibly busy week, and it's shaping up to be just as busy this weekend. I'll try to put in some serious time Sunday. Hopefully we'll get things running soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T05:31:29-07:00","id":284862,"title":"","content":"Found I had 2 pts left over...so purchased an RP thing. She now speaks the Minbari languages from Babylon 5. (technically, there are three, but ehh, it's a fictional language and all members of the species understood all three languages, just it was taboo to speak the wrong one)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1035366\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...heetid=1035366</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-17-2014, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T08:26:43-07:00","id":285937,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1029662\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...heetid=1029662</a><br /> <br /> Sheet modified to account for 27 XP. <br /> <br /> I love Spring Mantle 3, don't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T01:07:13-07:00","id":288415,"title":"","content":"Any word on when we're starting and where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T16:27:25-07:00","id":289090,"title":"","content":"I've been looking at some of the other sheets, and while the ST has the final say on the matter, I'm seeing a couple problems with 'em.<br /> <br /> Dwyad: First off, there's too many dots in the Mental Skills. The 5th dot in any Attribute or Skill costs 2 dots, so all in all you put in 13 dots at creation.<br /> <br /> Second, the Merit dots you purchased are a bit more expensive than what you put in your XP log(except for Quick Draw, that one's fine). See Merits cost &quot;New dots x 2&quot; and as misleading as &quot;New dots&quot; is, what they mean is that when you purchase a new dot, you have to spend XP for the entire dot value, not just the extra dot itself. For example, when purchasing the 2nd dot in Contacts, you have to spend 4 XP, not 2, because the new dot value you're getting is 2. Purchasing the 3rd dot in Allies costs 6 XP. Basically, the XP costs rise as you go up in dots. Also, you have to purchase the previous dot before you can get the next one.<br /> <br /> This means that getting the 2 dots in Contacts requires 6 XP(2 + 4), not 3. 3 dots in Allies requires 12 XP(2 + 4 + 6), not 6. You've spent a total of 36 XP, sorry. Other than that, you're fine.<br /> <br /> Thrythlind: First, getting an extra dot in Wyrd at creation doesn't cost 3 XP in addition to the Merit dot cost. Other than that, XP calculation is fine and dandy, so you have 3 extra XP to spend. Second, you also get a free Specialty in Athletics, Brawl, or Stealth at creation, and you start with 6 Glamour(it's rounded up, not down). Not really problems I guess, but I figured you should know anyways.<br /> <br /> The only real problem I can find is in the Contracts. You only get 5 dots at creation, not 7, and 3 XP is certainly not enough to cover the extra two dots.<br /> <br /> ATwannabe: I can't say because I can't see it.<br /> <br /> Like I said, ST has the final say, but I thought you guys should know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T17:17:13-07:00","id":289115,"title":"","content":"Whoops. Not sure how I got off on the contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T19:09:33-07:00","id":289165,"title":"","content":"Carp,<br /> <br /> Thanks! I hadn't gotten to the numbers yet - you're quite right! And actually, A'T... I can't see it either.<br /> <br /> Once we get the sheets hammered out, we're just about set - there's just a bit more info I'd like to see from each of your characters before we set up how we'll do the game OOC.<br /> <br /> Is your character new in Chicago, or established? If new, why're they coming into the Windy City? If established, are there any particular ties you think they'll have (family, business associates, friends, enemies)?<br /> <br /> I ask for this 'cuz it'll help me craft an opening that's a bit more nuanced than &quot;you all meet up in an inn.&quot;<br /> <br /> Regarding the methods for the game, I'd like to run via Google Drive - if you guys give me your google IDs (via PM or in the thread, your preference) I'll give you the link for the thread. Rolls will be done through <a href=\"http://www.invisiblecastle.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.invisiblecastle.com</a> - make sure you have a (free, no worries) account there!<br /> <br /> For formatting, I prefer prose rather than script, and folks may (but are not required to) use individual colors for dialogue for your characters. After you have a post, insert a line of five asterisks:<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> To indicate the cuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 10-21-2014, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T20:05:27-07:00","id":289188,"title":"","content":"I know how the Wyrd mix up happened. I took 3 pts off of merits and forgot it was off of merits not xp. <br /> <br /> As to contracts. Near as I can figure I noted it down at one point set the sheet down came back later and forgot I'd spent that XP. Hmmm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T21:35:29-07:00","id":289228,"title":"","content":"Actually....<br /> <br /> The fifth dot in an *attribute* costs double. (page 34) The fifth dot in a skill isn't called out at all, unless you have a source on that.<br /> <br /> And Spring Mantle 3 halves the XP costs of buying Allies and Contacts, so that's 1+2+3=6 and 1+2=3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwyad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=285937#post285937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love Spring Mantle 3, don't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Malory's a native - fetch drama is less dramatic if she only hears it on the news.<br /> <br /> She's set up in a low-rent apartment at the moment, and hasn't attempted to reconnect with anyone from her old life, knowing they'd think she's utterly mad. Instead, she frequently shows up at a domestic violence support group, occasionally talking about her Keeper in metaphorical terms, guiltily reaping bitter glamour, and sometimes forging short-term Pledges with her fellow victims. She's recently had a Dreaming Pledge with a woman named Erica Holder, soothing her entirely justified nightmares. Erica does not know Malory's nature, but she's a New Age believer, and is convinced that Malory knows how to make &quot;real&quot; dreamcatchers.<br /> <br /> On the less savory side, a young man named Isiah Cruz, no more than 16, regularly sees her trade money for prescription drugs. She's one of the few that actually uses them for their intended purpose, more or less. . The boy treats this with all the gravity of a summer job, and knows way too many faces for his age. He's a superstitious lad, and has seen a fair number of supposedly paranormal things. Malory has pressed, but has gotten little except wary glances and mutterings - &quot;speak of the devil&quot; isn't just a pithy phrase in his family, apparently.<br /> <br /> Still think this google doc thing is dodgy, but I've come this far. You can reach me at Dwyadicishness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3994,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","user":"Dwyad","date":". 10-22-2014, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T01:34:47-07:00","id":289375,"title":"","content":"google is <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#e2968a909b968a8e8b8c86a2858f838b8ecc818d8f\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"25514d575c514d494c4b41654248444c490b464a48\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><br /> <br /> Meaghan is a Chicago native, though her biological family is out in Colorado now, they have their mysterious wealth so they might conceivably show up at any given time. However, her fetch is in its 90s now, so less likely to travel. I leave the source of their funds up to the GM, it could be mundane back-room shenanigans, changeling pledges, demon pacts or any of a number of things. For all I know it has something to do with why Free was taken in the first place, or it could be completely different. Your call.<br /> <br /> Meaghan makes a fair amount of money off advertising on her site as well as the handful of people that donate or purchase her designed apps (she also has a few simple games out, but they're not catching on, partially because of her disconnect with humanity making them rather...odd). With Resources 1, she's a bit above the standard middle class so Meaghan lives in a converted, warehouse studio. It's low property value, not in the best of shape, but has room for her computer equipment. It's also often overlooked by the locals. She's considering looking into creating a Hollow for extra security, however.<br /> <br /> Most of Meaghan's contacts are online, though she does buy groceries from the same market every week and occasionally spends time at a local internet gaming cafe. She keeps inside her home as much as possible to avoid drawing local attention to it. She'd rather not have to deal with visitors of any stripe.<br /> <br /> Most of her contacts are online sources that she's used to plumb the depths of confusing lore and knowledge in the internet and try to glean some patterns that indicate supernatural events. In the course of this, she has gotten a limited reputation as a reputable and discrete source of information online for legitimate supernatural investigators. Of late, she's come to realize that some of the people she deals with are actually full out hunters and has become concerned about drawing attention. (I suspect she has at least one or two Network Zero types and possibly a Union type that she's had online encounters with, but, by and large she still just knows the tip of the iceberg when it comes to hunters) I paid points for this, but I expect it to be more of a complication or GM toy than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T01:38:33-07:00","id":289377,"title":"","content":"changes made to sheet: <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1035366\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...heetid=1035366</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T05:27:35-07:00","id":289453,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the notes, folks!<br /> <br /> Dwy, he's actually correct. Skills at 5 cost double just like attributes do - see bullet point 2 near the bottom of column 1 of page 34 in the core World of Darkness book.<br /> <br /> Thry, Dwy, both of you should have the invite. Let me know if you haven't gotten it yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 10-22-2014, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:02:33-07:00","id":289460,"title":"","content":"Ditched a dot of Medicine for a dot of Science, then, to broaden out my Knowin' Stuff skills.<br /> <br /> Confirming: invite arrived just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3994,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","user":"Dwyad","date":". 10-22-2014, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T13:41:17-07:00","id":289950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwyad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=289228#post289228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually....<br /> <br /> The fifth dot in an *attribute* costs double. (page 34) The fifth dot in a skill isn't called out at all, unless you have a source on that.<br /> <br /> And Spring Mantle 3 halves the XP costs of buying Allies and Contacts, so that's 1+2+3=6 and 1+2=3</div> </div> </div> </div>It says Skills cost two dots on that very page(same with Merits, too). As for the halving of Allies and Contacts, I didn't see that before(Only read up on the specifics of the Autumn Court for obvious reasons), sorry about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=289165#post289165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is your character new in Chicago, or established? If new, why're they coming into the Windy City? If established, are there any particular ties you think they'll have (family, business associates, friends, enemies)?<br /> <br /> I ask for this 'cuz it'll help me craft an opening that's a bit more nuanced than &quot;you all meet up in an inn&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, he's established as a respected member of both the Autumn Court and the Scarecrow Ministry and a damn good, albeit creepy, private detective as Nightshade. And as Sullivan, well...<br /> <br /> As far as any particular ties go, I've left the specifics to you. Just keep in mind that while he's not a complete anti-social lone wolf or anything, the majority of his interactions are strictly business and he doesn't make friends lightly. Very few know him by his actual name, as he very rarely gives it out. No one knows his true face because he keeps changing it(in fact, even he doesn't remember his original face, though he'll never admit it). Instead, people identify him by a special mark he creates, and it's a different one for each person or group. So while one person might identify him by a blemish on his face, another would identify him by a scar on his hand(when the motley forms, he'll have a mark everyone else will know by the way).<br /> <br /> Also, since he solves cases for changelings as well as mortals, it's perfectly fine for any of the other player characters to know him because he solved a case from them. Free could possibly know about him from his reputation in the Court but more likely from Sullivan. He could possibly approach Malory to ask her questions about one of her patients. Can't really think of anything else for Freddy though, considering he's a bridge troll(though I could think of something for the burnout lawyer, just saying).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=289165#post289165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the methods for the game, I'd like to run via Google Drive - if you guys give me your google IDs (via PM or in the thread, your preference) I'll give you the link for the thread. Rolls will be done through <a href=\"http://www.invisiblecastle.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.invisiblecastle.com</a> - make sure you have a (free, no worries) account there!</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'll go make an account of Invisible Castle then(would be pretty useful anyways) and I'll PM you my Gmail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T17:17:06-07:00","id":290114,"title":"","content":"Uh, how do I make the sheet public? I clicked &quot;public&quot; but then when I reload the page it is no longer checked.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetview.php?sheetid=1040756\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.myth-weavers.com/sheetvie...heetid=1040756</a><br /> <br /> EDIT: I clicked on that &quot;eye&quot; symbol. let me know if it worked...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2734,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","user":"ATwannabe","date":". 10-22-2014, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T17:27:02-07:00","id":290155,"title":"","content":"Freddy is a Chicago native, but he has been away for a while. First he was in the navy, and then he spent his durance in faerie under &quot;the captain.&quot; After his escape, he didn't know where else to go, so he drifted back home.<br /> <br /> Family is mostly gone, though his father might be out there somewhere, and as far as he knows there is no fetch, but he hasn't looked very hard. I envision his impact on the local culture to be relatively small - I purchased no allies or contacts, but I would think him a member of the local teamster's union, or perhaps just known well by other operators in the city. In addition, he would be polite to his neighbors, so they would recognize him, and he stops by a bar to tie one off after every shift, where he is a &quot;regular.&quot; Whether or not &quot;everybody knows your name&quot; there is another story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> He plays pool when he is there.<br /> <br /> In the freehold, he is known as a troll of considerable strength, and has helped many a changeling move a sofa, give them a lift in his truck, or rework their car's engine in exchange for glamour, favors, or goblin fruit.<br /> <br /> I had this typed up in my myth-weaver's sheet a while ago, but since it can't be read, here it is:<br /> Freddy has endured the life of the brutally abused, and has not been afraid to pay back in kind. He is not cruel, or evil, but in his own estimation, he is fair, maybe even level headed, regardless of what others say.<br /> <br /> His time in the Navy helped him get him training in engine and mechanical work, skills he is still proud of. It also gave him a place to vent his physical prowess in the boxing ring, both sanctioned and sub rosa.<br /> <br /> His durance under the Captain warped him into the monster of the deeps he is today. He is still drawn to the water, and likes to be near it, but knows that terrible things, even worse than him live down deep.<br /> <br /> Upon his return to Chicago, he never really tried to reclaim his old life \u2013 there wasn\u2019t much to claim anyway. He fell in with the winter court because it just made sense to him. There is sorrow in this life, and he has seen it and felt it.<br /> <br /> His whole life he has held onto the memory of his mother, lost to him. He sees her in his dreams sometimes, and it was her memory that he thinks preserved his mind amidst all those bloody tides. He is not meditative, and he is not crazy, but in moments of stress and panic he finds himself retreating mentally to his memories with her. Afterwards, he drowns in his emotions of missing her, and the life he thinks was robbed of him \u2013 not by his keeper, but by his dad. Dad did some time in prison, but Freddy has no idea what became of him. He just assumes he is out there somewhere. If he meets him, he\u2019ll drive a knife into his skull. But he doesn\u2019t think that dream will ever come true.<br /> <br /> So if I can't figure out the myth-weavers thing I'll type it all up and post it here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T17:31:28-07:00","id":290157,"title":"","content":"Anddddddd my third post: should we develop a motley pre-game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T20:42:55-07:00","id":290266,"title":"","content":"So. It looks like my work has not only blocked this forum, they've also blocked google drive. <br /> <br /> Which means that either we find another forum or program to play in that *isn't* blocked, or I can only post after work. Do any of you guys have preferences or ideas? <br /> <br /> If you guys want to work out backstory connections or even the full Motley, that'd work out. I can work you together in game, though, if you choose not to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T01:52:34-07:00","id":290376,"title":"","content":"PbP moves slowly, that's the nature of the thing, and no amount of effort will make it move quickly. The best we can do is make it move steadily.<br /> <br /> In PbP time, there's effectively no difference between posting at 4 o'clock and posting at 7 o'clock. The shortest viable measure of time is &quot;one day&quot;. So I suggest we use the forum we've got!<br /> <br /> As to connections? We've got a lot of Springs, so at the very least we've seen eachother at court functions. Anyone who's been wounded in ways they'd rather not explain to the hospital could probably know Malory. Both Dale and Free are time-lost, and could probably bond over that. <br /> <br /> Free, in particular, might have good reason to seek out a trustworthy doctor. Alien abductions usually involve strange experiments and implants, which might need to be extracted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T13:50:22-07:00","id":290757,"title":"","content":"I agree - I teach and therefore am up and moving and talking to students from the minute I start working until the last bell - I'm not sure if I can or cannot log on, but if I could I wouldn't have any time. I can check in the evenings, and even devote time for chats/posts but I'm in the same boat.<br /> <br /> Oh and I got the invite so I'm good to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T13:37:50-07:00","id":293166,"title":"","content":"Same, I teach, write and do a lot of live voice chat games...so my time is limited and a forum is as good as anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T23:45:44-07:00","id":293530,"title":"","content":"A'T, it looks like you're all good. To verify, the Union you have a contract with is your tollway worker's union, not the Hunter group, right?<br /> <br /> Dwyad, it looks like you're 3 XP over on your math. You missed one 1-dot skill (computer). Also, I was a bit thrown that the dot next to Quick Draw wasn't filled in - may wanna check on that!<br /> <br /> On a side note, Athletics isn't actually used for lifting - it's Strength + Stamina. That's why the Strong Back merit exists; it's essentially a Lifting specialty. You'll probably want to swap out your lifting spec for something else. Given your description of her escape, I'm thinking &quot;Running&quot; might be appropriate, or &quot;evading pursuit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Carp, it looks like you're fine on your XP; To clarify, is your specialization in&quot;Fae&quot; meant to indicate the True Fae or all fae creatures?<br /> <br /> Thry, I think your math looks okay, but I'm iffy on an occult spec in Hunters *and* contacts with Hunter organizations, especially as you say the character knows only &quot;just the tip of the iceburg&quot; when it comes to Hunterdom. <br /> <br /> Oh, and Cowardice isn't a Vice in this edition of the New World of Darkness. It has to be Sloth, Gluttony, Lust, Wrath, Pride, Greed, or Envy. Take a look at <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2/wod2.0/CreationVic.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2...eationVic.html</a> for the descriptions. I could see Sloth (avoiding danger or risk by making others do your work) or Envy (because that Fetch took your life, gorramit), but the choice is ultimately yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T00:40:01-07:00","id":293546,"title":"","content":"And is this thing happening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T02:34:51-07:00","id":293579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=293530#post293530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carp, it looks like you're fine on your XP; To clarify, is your specialization in&quot;Fae&quot; meant to indicate the True Fae or all fae creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's meant for all things fae and fae-related, whether they be changelings, True Fae, goblins, or the Hedge. Dale studied the subject quite a lot before he even went into the Hedge to verify that it was a possible enough lead. That, and he studied a lot more after his Durance(and with greater insight). Let me know if the Specialty is too broad.<br /> <br /> As for what the others have said about the schedule, I also agree. I don't mind if the game is a bit slow, so long as the pace is reasonably consistent. Also, it seems they might wanna go with the forums rather than a Google doc, and while I'm fine either way, I think it might be best to go with the forums simply because the majority of players seem to be comfortable with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T05:28:18-07:00","id":293641,"title":"","content":"Dwy, <br /> It is indeed! Presuming all the characters are up to date in time, I hope to have an introductory post up by Wednesday evening at the very latest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T17:02:07-07:00","id":294280,"title":"","content":"Hello. Yes - union was not meant to indicate the hunter group. Freddy is in the tollway worker's union. Excited - looking forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T18:24:31-07:00","id":295490,"title":"","content":"City background: The Freehold of Zephyr's Kiss<br /> <br /> Chicago has been a hub of transportation since long before the White Man showed up - it combines flat country (with easy access to ground travel) with access to the shipping lanes of the Great Lakes, and now boasts two major airports. The Lost know that this is true in the Hedge, as well. There are nearly half again as many Hedge Gates in Chicago as one might expect in a city of its size, and that's not even factoring in the suburbs. It's hard to keep track of all of those Hedge Gates and the Trods they open onto, and even the most diligent Autumn Rangers have only a fraction of them mapped. This easy access means that there are a large number of escaped Changelings who can find their ways home in Chicago, leading to a large, robust Freehold. Unfortunately, it also means that the Kindly Ones have an easy time finding new toys to replace the ones they lose. Nobody knows for certain how many people disappear from the streets every day, but some murmur that the number is distressingly high.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Freehold of Zephyr's Kiss tries to prevent such things, when it can. It's a very large Freehold, with more than 70 members to its name. The Courts seem relatively evenly represented - although in the case of Winter, that's mostly speculation. The Freehold maintains a massive Hollow in the Hedge: a massive castle, shaped like the Sears Tower (no local Chicagoan will call it the Willis Tower, no matter what's on the label) but at least a mile in height. The castle's spire wavers in the wind, but never seems quite unbalanced enough to fall.<br /> <br /> The Summer King of Chicago is Maxim Katch, an Ogre Render with heavy ties to the city's unions, especially the construction workers' union. He does his best to make sure that construction stays as troublesome as possible, feasting on the road rage and trusting to the Hedge for transportation. His court is relatively laissez faire, as Summer goes. He makes sure every member has a burner cell phone on them at all times. If that phone rings, you'd better answer it and do what he says. Otherwise, he rarely interferes.<br /> <br /> Leading the Autumn Court is a figure known only as the Nameless. A tall, skeletally thin figure in hedgespun robes of shadow and terror, the Nameless never lets anybody see his face. Twenty years ago, he met in parley with one of the True Fae as a member of the Legacy of the Black Apple. Nobody knows what they discussed, but the Fae and his Armies left the next day, and from then on nobody could remember the Nameless's face or name. He spends most of his time in the Autumn Court's own Hollow, a sprawling cavern complex. His lieutenant, a twin-kithed Darkling Antiquarian and Gravewight known as Anthony Malcalling, handles most of the day-to-day business of the Court - though Anthony insists that he has no wish to take the crown.<br /> <br /> Winter's queen, White Lucy, keeps her court organized like a subversive cell. While some of the members are easily recognizable as Winter due to the strength of their Mantle or a lack of ability to disguise the signs in their Mein, a surprising number masquerade as Courtless Lost, Ensorcelled mortals - or even, many suspect, as false members of the other Courts. Each Winter courtier only knows the true identity of a small handful of these hidden members - only White Lucy knows all of them. While the other courts look askance at some of Winter's methods, they can't deny that the myriad bolt-holes and hidden supply dumps the court maintains have saved lives and freedom many times before.<br /> <br /> The Spring King, Larry Hoggs, owns an italian beef truck - and keeps track on his court from the streets. A fat, jovial Broadback Beast, King Larry is everyone's best friend, always free with a sandwich and a smile for members of the Freehold. His cheerful manner and frequently-stained shirts hide a keener mind than many expect from his Court and Seeming, and it's said that he has uncalled favors and ongoing pledges with high-ranking members of all three of the other Courts. Larry's also a part-owner of a number of bars, restaurants, and clubs throughout the city, and each one has a room somewhere that the Lost can meet in unmolested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 10-29-2014, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T09:09:46-07:00","id":295901,"title":"","content":"Sheet's fix'd, lost a point of underworld contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T20:45:34-07:00","id":296507,"title":"","content":"OK. Got the first post ready to put up as soon as I get confirmation from Thry. Dwy, are you going to keep the Lifting spec, or would you like to swap it out for something that'll see more use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T21:05:45-07:00","id":296519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thry, I think your math looks okay, but I'm iffy on an occult spec in Hunters *and* contacts with Hunter organizations, especially as you say the character knows only &amp;quot;just the tip of the iceburg&amp;quot; when it comes to Hunterdom. <br /> <br /> Oh, and Cowardice isn't a Vice in this edition of the New World of Darkness. It has to be Sloth, Gluttony, Lust, Wrath, Pride, Greed, or Envy. Take a look at <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2/wod2.0/CreationVic.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2...eationVic.html</a> for the descriptions. I could see Sloth (avoiding danger or risk by making others do your work) or Envy (because that Fetch took your life, gorramit), but the choice is ultimately yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cowardice is listed as an alternate version of Sloth in the original WoD core book and is more accurate so I went with that. <br /> <br /> As to the contacts, I'll switch it to gamers. Makes things easier. <br /> <br /> And then I'm ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T06:55:00-07:00","id":297077,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/296605-changeling-the-lost-unseen-costs-ic\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...nseen-costs-ic</a> !<br /> <br /> Game on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 10-30-2014, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T19:42:01-07:00","id":298636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/266607-recruiting-for-a-play-by-post-changeling-the-lost-chronicle?p=279252#post279252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with the Shadowsoul is that it gets 3 kith benefits, where most get one or two at most. In addition, several of those benefits are more powerful than other kiths' entire benefit, let alone singular powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>In game, I've never had one be &quot;too powerful&quot;. All of them are how you play them really. A muse, with the right connection, can rule the world in the background of a powerful man/woman for instance. Is there room for one more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T22:07:22-07:00","id":298684,"title":"","content":"Not right now, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T23:51:49-07:00","id":298705,"title":"","content":"&quot;A Perception roll&quot; is Wits+Composure, but what's &quot;a Stamina roll&quot; in this context? Just Stamina? Stamina+Resolve? Stamina+Athletics? <br /> <br /> And, though I'd rather not bring a debate to the OOC thread, yeah, I don't buy &quot;all kiths are equally broken&quot;. All kiths CAN be broken with enough GM favor, but some clearly require more favor than others. For example, it's much easier to use &quot;scary&quot; or &quot;alluring&quot; or &quot;really perceptive&quot; in the context of a typical game than it is to use &quot;able to endure poison, slightly better at scavenging.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Roteater can still be effective, by, say, preparing a poisoned meal for an enemy and eating with him to prove it's safe, but opportunities to do that just aren't going to come up as often as opportunities to talk to people or notice things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T08:59:55-07:00","id":298976,"title":"","content":"In this case, just Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T09:51:26-07:00","id":299017,"title":"","content":"What dice roller do we use again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T09:52:28-07:00","id":299018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.InvisibleCastle.com\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\